  "analysis": "Both responses outline a multi‑lane plan with gates and required approvals, but MTV correctly respects the read‑only config constraint, proposes a feature‑flag rollback to avoid the costly full database restore, and explicitly handles the flaky network‑latency check. JFT misinterprets the config lock (suggesting jobs run outside business hours to keep the config writable) and relies on a full restore as the primary rollback, which is riskier. MTV therefore gives a more accurate, safer, and lower‑overhead path to the requested idempotent ingestion fix.",
